{:db/id "q-161104" :question/id #uuid "d8ed3010-dff4-51a2-aca7-aa8cacfdb425" :question/math-academy-id "q-161104" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/059cec995f7ef75b56b8c512af09051fe4631733e87d98d25065144500613f73.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $17{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{46}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 63\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{46}^{∘} \\\\  & =22.659… \\\\  & ≈23{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =23-17 \\\\  & =6{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161104/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161104"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161109/selection/3942fbcd53b2b9ad05e96f1486373ebac198bab8ad7a4c7776b1a1273d298766" :answer/id #uuid "912c8688-c2f9-51d1-b753-42c7c7830a6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161109/selection/1260a496c664ed4d56ca47ecd044784002e5eaad4a1041ed055c852ed16f0608" :answer/id #uuid "d99ce202-bf1b-59b0-9790-dc8037fbdc7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161109/selection/ba8f8c88e77e66a95d43babdf55fa7580d6c7eb995a910ec65313ef90dd74868" :answer/id #uuid "f6d0fa2c-295e-5aaa-ae81-010af2790b7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161109/selection/e6227308a56c2eaed114c1bf55b29ff6407c20ea63ba28b95e775a3d1b0f89a7" :answer/id #uuid "aa985a76-a9b9-5b69-840b-0742526df5af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161109/selection/caa2ea618c6246cec38b223991306a64c9e6f5b6ee6d7f76367c84a3b2abd6c1" :answer/id #uuid "97682d06-c845-592f-9f69-d2a728b91a58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161109/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "156f3f94-c03f-5e25-846d-ab87c7a8f0ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161109/selection/3942fbcd53b2b9ad05e96f1486373ebac198bab8ad7a4c7776b1a1273d298766" :answer-field/choices ["q-161109/selection/3942fbcd53b2b9ad05e96f1486373ebac198bab8ad7a4c7776b1a1273d298766" "q-161109/selection/1260a496c664ed4d56ca47ecd044784002e5eaad4a1041ed055c852ed16f0608" "q-161109/selection/ba8f8c88e77e66a95d43babdf55fa7580d6c7eb995a910ec65313ef90dd74868" "q-161109/selection/e6227308a56c2eaed114c1bf55b29ff6407c20ea63ba28b95e775a3d1b0f89a7" "q-161109/selection/caa2ea618c6246cec38b223991306a64c9e6f5b6ee6d7f76367c84a3b2abd6c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161109" :question/id #uuid "3f5486d5-f842-5cab-abfe-caf15b80d4f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161109" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/b95571772af958b4f7b7dcdbba630b78e029c838340dc272809a6c7915dc9c90.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=6\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 6\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}\\,b}{2} \\\\ \\frac{21\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}}{\\cancel{2}} & =\\frac{3\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}\\,b}{\\cancel{2}} \\\\ 3b & =21 \\\\ b & =7\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=7\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161109/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161109"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279762/field-1/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" :answer/id #uuid "fdc387d7-8c8c-581a-a9d6-703f80eb0fc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279762/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "709258f2-84c2-5384-b559-2a3be2dd0ec4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279762/field-1/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" :answer-field/choices ["q-279762/field-1/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279762" :question/id #uuid "7534130c-7b66-543d-b26d-a4a7b4a429a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-279762" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/54265327c77bedb300fe0d1f1f08ca3ab2d7ae37f35f49007d3f20ab3a21dbaa.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/b1d0cf7c5a7c6ad7f0f52c8686239920fabcb05be57372ae0c7c9c9491838a52.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(10)(6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈25.981,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 25.981 \\\\  & =51.962.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $52.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279762/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279762"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280282/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "55db0fbe-c27d-5d05-b585-851aa55b2dc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280282/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "0ab95a5b-1a0f-5c4b-b9e3-6d0cd5cc5526" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280282/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa7aff40-0fe9-5c3f-a695-745f3d50bfb6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280282/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-280282/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" "q-280282/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280282" :question/id #uuid "f42a4731-18b0-562d-a10b-9dc0dd292374" :question/math-academy-id "q-280282" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/5c0bf3060129e2a03dab0fcd2a6f0f6068d1ec565143b83d11ad4d8ae1b41b85.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the acute triangle $△ABC$ is $3{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$ Then, the measure of $∠A$ is{{field-1}} ${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{ mm}, \\\\ b & =AC=4\\,\\text{mm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 3 & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-280282/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280282"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-285740/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "43743b66-55b2-5c32-8c3e-0c7909593dc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-285740/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fb8c0dd-ad7a-5ea4-a5da-2dc24ac1c91c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-285740/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-285740/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-285740" :question/id #uuid "4c12c505-999a-5051-95ac-753d9f8950cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-285740" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/b69082ef86283bc842ce487b62901e8946ffff53ab8323a6fc846f68c5869aae.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $10{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{cm}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 24\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘} \\\\  & =11.591… \\\\  & ≈12{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-285740/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-285740"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
